WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
At the beginning of the movie, Nurse Marion, the&nbsp;
same nurse from the original Halloween, sends her teenage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.120
neighbor Jimmy to investigate a break-in at&nbsp;
her house. He proceeds to raid her fridge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.880
where we can see a six-pack of Penn Pavel’s beer&nbsp;
on the shelf. This fictional beer company can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.360
be spotted in many films and TV shows; The Truman&nbsp;
Show, Donnie Darko and The Walking Dead, are a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.920
examples. But what is the reason for this? What is&nbsp;
the connection between these seemingly random IPs?

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.400
It goes back to the specialty&nbsp;
print shop, The Earl Hays Press,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.760
who produced this beverage prop as a neutral&nbsp;
brand for several different productions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.280
The Earl Hays Press is most known for creating&nbsp;
fake news articles for Hollywood. We see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.880
lot of this during the opening titles&nbsp;
for Halloween H20: 20 Years Later, or,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.880
as I’ll be referring to it for the rest of&nbsp;
this video for my time and your sanity, H2O.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.520
I know this breaks my usual schtick of exact&nbsp;
pronunciations, but I’m gonna call it H2O because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.520
that’s how my brain interprets it. These articles&nbsp;
contain some interesting details… to learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.360
about that, plus all the ways that this movie&nbsp;
interacted with the Scream franchise, who this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.080
lady really is, plus many other easter eggs and&nbsp;
secrets, stick around to the end of this video.

